GitHub + Git Bash + EC2 + GitHub Actions — Step-by-Step Guide
1. Create a GitHub Account
1. Go to https://github.com
2. Click 'Sign up'.
3. Enter your email, password, and username.
4. Verify your email address.
5. Log in to your account.
2. Install and Connect Git Bash
1. Download Git from https://git-scm.com/downloads
2. Install with default settings.
3. Open Git Bash from the Start menu.
Set up your name and email:

git config --global user.name "Your Name"
git config --global user.email "your_email@example.com"
git config --list

3. Generate SSH Key (for GitHub)

ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -C "your_email@example.com"
eval "$(ssh-agent -s)"
ssh-add ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
cat ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub
ssh -T git@github.com

4. GitHub Repository Commands

git clone git@github.com:username/repository-name.git
cd repository-name
git status
git add .
git commit -m "commit message"
git push origin main
git pull origin main

5. Create & Connect to AWS EC2 Instance

# Change directory to .pem key location
cd path/to/key

# Change key permissions
chmod 400 your-key.pem

# Connect to EC2
ssh -i "your-key.pem" ubuntu@ec2-xx-xx-xx-xx.compute-1.amazonaws.com

6. Generate New SSH Key for GitHub Actions Deployment

ssh-keygen -t rsa -b 4096 -C "github-actions"
cat ~/.ssh/id_rsa.pub
mkdir -p ~/.ssh
echo "paste-public-key-here" >> ~/.ssh/authorized_keys
chmod 600 ~/.ssh/authorized_keys

7. GitHub Actions Secrets Setup
Add the following secrets in GitHub repository → Settings → Secrets → Actions:
• EC2_HOST → Public IP of EC2 instance
• EC2_USER → ubuntu
• EC2_KEY → Paste full private key from id_rsa
8. Sample GitHub Actions Workflow File

name: CI/CD Deploy to EC2

on:
  push:
    branches: [ main ]

jobs:
  deploy:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest

    steps:
      - name: Checkout Code
        uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - name: Setup SSH
        uses: webfactory/ssh-agent@v0.7.0
        with:
          ssh-private-key: ${{ secrets.EC2_KEY }}

      - name: Deploy to EC2
        run: |
          ssh -o StrictHostKeyChecking=no ${{ secrets.EC2_USER }}@${{ secrets.EC2_HOST }} << 'EOF'
            cd /var/www/html
            git pull origin main
            pm2 restart all || true
          EOF

9. Verify and Test

git add .
git commit -m "Testing GitHub Actions deployment"
git push origin main
